    {
      "id": "animals",
      "icon": "🐕",
      "title": "Animals",
      "subtitle": "L-annimali: male, female and more than one",
      "intro": "Living things carry three forms, exactly like the jobs you learned last time: male, female, and the plural. The plural is often a different word again.",
      "facts": [
        "The feminine is usually the masculine plus -a: kelb becomes kelba, qattus becomes qattusa.",
        "The plural rarely follows that pattern. Kelb becomes klieb and qattus becomes qtates, rebuilt from the inside.",
        "Farm animals often use two different words for male and female, the way English has bull and cow."
      ],
